  "harnessFindings": [
    "The first preparation observer required an empty native-call list. A retained incoming object was positively terminated; no active call or bearer was present. That read-only attempt timed out before any maintenance write. Its evidence was archived, and the helper was corrected to accept only positively terminated history while retaining exact original equipment/SIM and active-call checks.",
    "A bounded read observer retained a transient HTTP line_busy response; it recovered before answering, without another application start or answer submission.",
    "The initial packet analyzer classified some RTCP packets as RTP. Compound RTCP framing was separated before publication; no carrier call was repeated for this analysis repair.",
    "The observer initially named final teardown as handset hangup. The actual SIP dialog and Baresip log show that the 40-second source reached EOF and the winning endpoint sent BYE. The final report corrects that label and retains the original observer result privately.",
    "The actual receiving client WAV contains 10.481 seconds of decoded audio; raw captured PCMA payloads decode to 10.58 seconds. Three of four inspected one-second client blocks occur exactly in the captured decode. Full byte equality is false and its cause is not established; lossless/full-call audio identity is not claimed."
  ],
